# --- OS ---
.DS_Store

# --- FinScreen data cache ---
# data/raw/ holds cached raw EDGAR JSON responses (submissions dumps, filing
# indices, the bulk ticker map). It is fully regenerable by re-running the
# ingestion script against data/universe.csv (idempotent, same rate-limited
# client) and can grow to tens/hundreds of MB across the universe, so it is
# excluded from version control rather than committed.
#
# data/universe.csv IS versioned deliberately -- it's the locked, hand-chosen
# company list and is not regenerable from anything else.
#
# data/filings_metadata.db (SQLite) is a small, deterministic derived
# artifact (a few thousand rows of filing metadata) -- it is NOT excluded
# here so the ingested metadata snapshot is reproducible/inspectable without
# re-hitting EDGAR, but if it grows large in later weeks this choice should
# be revisited.
data/raw/

# --- Bulk / regenerable artifacts (added for public GitHub push) ---
# Batch API request payloads: ~308 MB across variants, three of them 77 MB
# each (over GitHub's 50 MB warning threshold). Fully regenerable by
# re-running build_batch_requests.py against data/labeling_corpus.parquet.
data/*.jsonl

# Derived text/price corpora. Regenerable from data/raw/ via extract.py +
# chunk.py, and from the price client, respectively.
data/filings.parquet
data/labeling_corpus.parquet
data/prices.parquet
data/paragraph_occurrence_map.parquet

# Bootstrap label sets. NOTE: unlike everything else here, these are NOT
# free to regenerate -- they cost real Batch API spend. They are excluded to
# keep the repo lean, which means git is NOT a backup for them. Keep an
# independent copy. To version them instead, delete the four lines below.
data/labels.parquet
data/labels_pre_relabel.parquet
data/labels_relabel.parquet
data/labels_corrective.parquet

# Fine-tune datasets: 41 MB, deterministically derived from labels.parquet
# via finetune/prepare_dataset.py and finetune/split.py (seeded splits).
finetune/prepared/
finetune/splits/
